cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "gpuGEM: GPU-based solving of linear optimisation problems over genome-scale metabolic models"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Digital-Metabolic-Twin-Centre/gpuGEM"
abstract: >-
  gpuGEM solves the linear programmes arising in constraint-based modelling of
  genome-scale metabolic networks on NVIDIA GPUs, wrapping the cuOpt PDLP
  first-order solver behind a COBRA-compatible interface. It includes an
  application that prioritises candidate inherited-metabolic-disease genes from
  a patient's blood biomarker pattern using the Harvey whole-body model.
keywords:
  - flux balance analysis
  - genome-scale metabolic model
  - linear programming
  - GPU
  - PDLP
  - cuOpt
  - COBRA
  - systems biology
  - inherited metabolic disease
